#: includes/settings.php:1020
msgid "Enable Author Box"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1024
msgid ""
"An author box is a great way to credit authors by displaying their "
"information on posts. Customize its appearance and choose specific post "
"types for automatic or manual display. Disable this option only if you don't "
"want to show any author boxes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1036
msgid "Enable Guest Authors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1040
msgid ""
"Allow guest authors to be credited on your site without needing a user "
"account. Enabling this setting lets you add profiles for guest authors, "
"showcasing their contributions on selected post types without granting them "
"access to the WordPress Dashboard. Use this to highlight contributors who "
"don't have a regular login, such as freelancers or occasional writers. If "
"disabled, guest author profiles will not be available.."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1052
msgid "Enable Co-Authors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1056
msgid ""
"Enable the option to credit multiple authors on a single post, making it "
"easy to recognize collaborative work. When enabled, you can configure which "
"post types support multiple authors, allowing you to assign joint credit on "
"selected content types. If disabled, only one author will be associated with "
"each post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1068
msgid "Enable Custom Author Avatars"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1072
msgid ""
"Allow custom profile images for authors, offering a personalized look that "
"isn’t tied to Gravatar. Enabling this option lets you upload unique images "
"for each author’s avatar, giving you greater control over visual branding "
"and profile presentation on your site. If disabled, author avatars will rely "
"on Gravatar images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1080
msgid "Enable Enhanced Author Profile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1084
msgid ""
"Add more fields to author profiles to display detailed information like "
"telephone, job position, company, and social network links. This option "
"allows you to provide richer author bios, enhancing credibility and "
"connection with readers. When enabled, you can configure and showcase "
"additional information for each author. If disabled, only basic profile "
"information will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1109
msgid "Change Default Author"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1113
msgid ""
"Set one or more default authors for new posts, ideal for sites where posts "
"are commonly attributed to specific authors or teams. When enabled, a search "
"box will let you select default authors, simplifying the assignment process. "
"If disabled, WordPress will continue with its default behavior, assigning "
"the current user as the author on new posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1125
msgid "Manage User Roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1129
msgid ""
"Control which User Roles can be assigned as authors for posts, providing "
"flexibility in post attribution. This setting is especially useful for sites "
"with custom roles or collaborative content workflows, allowing you to expand "
"authoring capabilities beyond standard roles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1141
msgid "Enable Post Contributors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1145
msgid ""
"Recognize and showcase the talents behind your content! Add custom "
"attributions—reviewers, fact-checkers, editors, photographers, and more—and "
"display them alongside the post author. Elevate transparency and give credit "
"where it's due."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1160
msgid "Enable Posting as Other Authors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1161
msgid ""
"Allow users without specific permissions to publish content on behalf of "
"other authors. This setting is useful for collaborative sites where roles "
"outside of editors or admins may need to assign posts to designated authors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1172
msgid "Hide Posts From Other Authors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1173
msgid ""
"Limit selected user roles to viewing only their own posts in the Dashboard, "
"helping authors focus on their content and keeping their post lists concise "
"and manageable. This setting is ideal for maintaining privacy and minimizing "
"distractions in collaborative environments. If disabled, all users can view "
"posts from other authors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1200
msgid "Customize Post Byline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1206
msgid ""
"The byline on a post gives the name of the people who contributed to write "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1221
msgid "Customize Author Box Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1227
msgid ""
"Enable this option to access and adjust the author box display settings for "
"posts across your site. Please note that some of these display settings "
"might be overridden by specific configurations set at the individual post or "
"author level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1242
msgid "Enable Author Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1248
msgid ""
"Enable this option to access and adjust the author box display settings for "
"posts across your site. Please note that these display settings might be "
"overridden by specific configurations set at the individual post or author "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1263
msgid "Enable Enhanced Search Functionality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1269
msgid ""
"Enable this option to activate advanced search options, including searching "
"content by author name and displaying guest author archives in search "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1284
msgid "Encode Sensitive Author Information"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1290
msgid ""
"Enable this option to encode sensitive information to make it unreadable to "
"SPAM bots."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1320
msgid "Enable Social Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1326
msgid ""
"Enable to configure social profiles for authors and select which social "
"networks to include."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1340
msgid "Enable SEO Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1346
msgid ""
"Enable to access settings for managing schema markup and meta tags to "
"enhance SEO."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:1361
msgid "Enable REST API Integration"
